id: DRAFT-E-libzip19-source-callback
severity: 2
category: dependency, conan, linking
trigger_tool: conan
phase: runtime|test
approach: replace hand-rolled zip_source_make_command_bitmap with official ZIP_SOURCE_SUPPORTS_SEEKABLE and return 0 for unhandled callback commands

keywords: libzip, zip_source_function_create, zip_source_make_command_bitmap, ZIP_SOURCE_SUPPORTS, ZIP_ER_OPNOTSUPP, zip_err 28, zip_open_from_source, callback, OPNOTSUPP, source callback, lib3mf, OPC

error_signature: zip_open_from_source.*failed|ZIP_ER_OPNOTSUPP|zip_err=28|Error in libzip callback|COULDNOTREADZIPFILE
match_keywords: zip_source_function_create, ZIP_ER_OPNOTSUPP, zip_err=28, zip_open_from_source, ZIP_SOURCE_SUPPORTS_SEEKABLE

root_cause: >
  Libraries written against libzip < 1.9 (e.g. lib3mf 1.8.1's bundled
  NMR_OpcPackageReader) implement custom zip source callbacks with a
  hand-rolled capability bitmap built from zip_source_make_command_bitmap(
  OPEN, READ, CLOSE, STAT, ERROR, SEEK, TELL, SUPPORTS, -1) and throw an
  exception for unknown commands in the default branch. libzip >= 1.9
  (verified on 1.11.4) requires additional command bits inside
  zip_open_from_source; the old bitmap makes open fail with
  ZIP_ER_OPNOTSUPP (zip_err=28) even though the archive itself is valid.
  Additionally libzip >= 1.9 issues newer commands
  (ZIP_SOURCE_GET_FILE_ATTRIBUTES, ZIP_SOURCE_ACCEPT_EMPTY, ...) to
  callback sources; an exception-throwing default branch aborts the
  process at runtime.

affected_scope: any consumer of zip_source_function_create/zip_open_from_source migrating from libzip < 1.9 to >= 1.9

rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: >
  1) Replace the hand-rolled bitmap in the ZIP_SOURCE_SUPPORTS case with
  the official capability macro: return ZIP_SOURCE_SUPPORTS_SEEKABLE.
  2) Change the callback default branch from throwing/returning -1 to
  returning 0 for unhandled commands.
  3) Verify with a write-then-read round-trip of the consumer's file
  format (the write path often uses zip_open and still works; only the
  read path via zip_open_from_source breaks).
rec_description: patch the consumer's zip source callback (not libzip itself)
rec_command: >
  sed -i 's/zip_source_make_command_bitmap(.*,-1);/ZIP_SOURCE_SUPPORTS_SEEKABLE;/'
  and change default: throw CNMRException(...) to default: return 0;
  then rebuild and run the package round-trip test.
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: manual

fallback: if the consumer cannot be patched, pin libzip to a < 1.9 release (loses security fixes; not recommended)

verify_builds: 46345

doc_file: knowledge/drafts/DRAFT-E-libzip19-source-callback.md
prescriptions: P-DEP-001 dependency family upgrade awareness

authors: j669539
